# Qualification findings for layerx-merge v2: one [finding.<N>.<k>.<m>] per finding, keyed by the v2 task id that met it; a second finding for the same task is [finding.<N>.<k>.<m>.<n>].
# Keys, in this order (spec/workflow.kvx [qualification_log] entry_keys): task, file, symbol, observed, assumption, severity.
# Format source: spec/workflow.kvx [qualification_log] and [loop] step_6. Path of this ledger: spec/layerx-merge/qualification.kvx.
#   task       = "<N>.<k>.<m>"  the v2 task whose qualification exposed the finding
#   file       = "<repo-relative path>:<line>"  where the failure or contradiction is observed
#   symbol     = "<exact identifier: test, function, error code, selector or key>"
#   observed   = "<one sentence naming revision, exact command, exit code and log path, then what failed>"
#   assumption = "<one sentence: the assumption the task proceeds on>"
#   severity   = "blocker" | "suspect" | "assumption" | "note"
# Append when: You hit an unrelated or pre-existing failure, a contradiction between requirements or tasks, a missing external interface, or a repair that would require weakening a check. Append once; never append the same finding twice.
# Never: Do not log a task-scoped failure as an excuse to skip repair. Do not write narrative: observed is one sentence, assumption is one sentence, and every entry names revision, exact command, exit code and log path. An entry over six lines is a defect.
# An entry is exactly the six keys above (six lines); append once and never re-run or re-investigate a recorded finding.
#
# The v2 specification starts clean: this ledger holds no findings at revision 2a1033aa2.
# The 330 findings of the previous ledger were recorded against v1 task ids of the stale specification and are not carried forward.
# Superseded findings: previous-ledger finding ids whose recorded gap is now a v2 task (previous id -> v2 task, reason).
#   5.0.8 -> 11.15.1: interop lock check; decision.1101 records the finding as not reproduced at HEAD
#   5.0.9 -> 16.7.4: build_cmd is bash -n tools/bringup/xweb-config.sh
#   7.0.7 -> 17.6.1: solidity sandbox profile runs contracts/bridge/evm/bootstrap-libs.sh before forge
#   12.0.2 -> 16.38.1: OCC harness loads cw20_base.wasm instead of mars.wasm (decision.1628)
#   10.0.4 -> 6.91.1: arbiter codes -737..-739 registered in the LXP error registry
#   0.111 -> 7.10.1: newHeads key set aligned with eth_getBlockByNumber
#   5.1.2 -> 6.65.1: IXWeb.sol names the three origin-2 methods
#   gateway.lx-reads-wait-on-ingress-off -> 8.3.1: every lx_ name answers -32601
#   4.3.4 -> 13.22.1: 0x101D executor, merge constructor and dispatch table
#   8.5.24 -> 8.47.3: streaming conformance resumes logs by (blockHeight, txIndex, logIndex)
#   13.3.3 -> 1.20.2: linked escrow arbiter rule with LXP_ERR_UNAUTHORIZED_ARBITER
#   1.2.2 -> 6.3.2: paused-denom bank send reverts with LXP_ASSET_PAUSED
#   0.1 -> 6.6.9: unread PrecompileLastUpgrade retired
#   1.1.3 -> 1.39.3: kernel account rows checked against the Go codec account kinds
#   10.0.2 -> 6.7.3: activation addresses without a custom precompile reported
